lished: 3.0 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; This paper proves Brown and Erey's conjecture that $2$-connected $k$-chromatic graphs with $n$ vertices have at most $(x-1)_{k-1}\\big((x-1)^{n-k+1}+(-1)^{n-k}\\big)$ proper $x$-colorings for $x\\geq k$, under the condition that either the graph's clique number is $k$ or its independent number is $2$. ... @article{yang2023some, title = {Some results on the maximal chromatic polynomials of $2$-connected $k$-chromatic graphs}, author = {Yang, Yan}, year = {2023}, eprint = {2310.16382}, archivePrefix = {arXiv}, primaryClass = {math.CO}, }\n\nBack ArXiv math.CO Some results on the maximal chromatic polynomials of $2$-connected $k$-chromatic graphs\n\nArXiv math.CO\n\n# Some results on the maximal chromatic polynomials of $2$-connected $k$-chromatic graphs\n\nYan Yang\n\n2310.16382 Published Oct 26, 2023\n\nChat with paper Cite 中文 View PDF Share\n\n### Publication\n\nPublished: Oct 26, 2023\n\nCategories: math.CO\n\n### Metrics\n\nSource: ArXiv\n\n### AI Quick Summary\n\nThis paper proves Brown and Erey's conjecture that $2$-connected $k$-chromatic graphs with $n$ vertices have at most $(x-1)_{k-1}\\big((x-1)^{n-k+1}+(-1)^{n-k}\\big)$ proper $x$-colorings for $x\\geq k$, under the condition that either the graph's clique number is $k$ or its independent number is $2$. This extends previous results proving the conjecture for $x=k$.\n\n### Paper Preview\n\n### Abstract\n\nIn 2015, Brown and Erey conjectured that every $2$-connected graph $G$ on $n$ vertices with chromatic number $k\\geq 4$ has at most $(x-1)_{k-1}\\big((x-1)^{n-k+1}+(-1)^{n-k}\\big)$ proper $x$-colorings for all $x\\geq k$. Engbers, Erey, Fox, and He proved this conjecture for $x=k$. In this paper, we prove Brown and Erey's conjecture under the condition that either the clique number of $G$ is $k$, or the independent number of $G$ is $2$.\n\n### OpenAlex\n\nCitations in OpenAlex\n    0\n\nPublication year\n    2023\n\nAccess status\n    Open access\n\nView on Op