l arbitrary graphs and $\\boxtimes$⊠ denotes the strong product of graphs. This article delves into various critical theorems regarding the computation of this number. Specifically, we address its NP-hardness and the complexity of approximating it. Furthermore, we develop a conjecture for necessary and sufficient conditions for this number to be less than one. We also validate this conjecture for specific graph families. Additionally, we present miscellaneous concepts and introduce a generalized version of the independence number that gives insights that could significantly contribute to the study of the relative fractional packing number.\n\n@misc{taziki2023relativefractionalpackingnumber, title={Relative Fractional Packing Number and Its Properties}, author={Mehrshad Taziki}, year={2023}, eprint={2311.16390}, archivePrefix={arXiv}, primaryClass={math.CO}, url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.16390}, }--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Taziki_M in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3ATaziki_M+in%3Amath)\nciteturn3search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; @misc{2311.16390, author = {Mehrshad Taziki}, title = {{R}elative {F}ractional {P}acking {N}umber and {I}ts {P}roperties}, year = {2023}, eprint = {2311.16390}, note = {arXiv:2311.16390v1} }[Button: Copy Citation] ... Furthermore, we develop a conjecture for necessary and sufficient conditions for this number to be less than one. ... Additionally, we present miscellaneous concepts and introduce a generalized version of the independence number that gives insights that could significantly contribute to the study of the relative fractional packing number.\n# Search SciRate\n\n2 results for au:Taziki_M in:math\n\nShow all abstracts\n\n  * Relative Fractional Packing Number and Its Properties\n\nMehrshad Taziki\n\nNov 29 2023 math.CO cs.IT math.IT arXiv:2311.16390v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{2311.16390, author = {Mehrshad Taz